@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ The day page, at `/framework/ai/<YYYY-MM-DD>/`: every task of the day as a check
 
 | Piece | Job |
 |---|---|
-| `AIDay.js` (`AIDay extends View`) | asks the `tasks` source for `day == this day`, builds the tree from each row's folder path, repaints on every pushed row |
+| `AIDay.js` (`AIDay extends View`) | asks the `tasks` source twice, for `landed_day == this day` (work that landed today in an older session's folder) and then `day == this day` (this day's folders; asked last, because the server pushes changed rows for the last query only), builds the tree from each row's folder path, repaints on every pushed row |
 | `AIDay.css` | `aid-` rules, one column at 400 px |
 | `Server/SessionIndex.mjs` | registers the `tasks` query source over the sessions store; whether a task landed is `AIIndex.fold`'s call, never this page's |
 
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@ Data path: `sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/**/task.jsonl|session.jsonl` → `SessionIndex`
 ## Watch out
 
 - Needs the dev server (a static host has no socket); the page says so.
-- A task that landed on this day from an older day's folder is not listed (the query is by folder day).
+- A task counts as landed only when its own record says so (`complete`, or a landing line from `finish-task`); a minion's `ready:` line or a parent's log line is not a landing.
+- A session from an older day shows its start day beside its name and links to its own dated folder.
 - Spend is shown only when a row carries `usd`; task rows rarely do, so most days show none.
 - A depth-1 folder of the day is a session; every row below it is a task.
diff --git a/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md b/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
index 241d7643f..0fc6888b1 100644
--- a/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
+++ b/public/framework/ai/AISession/readme.md
@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@
 
 - `AISession.js` — one session's cost, read from its raw transcript (browser and node).
 - `AISessionsPage.js` · `AISessionView.js` · `AISessionRows.js` · `AISessionBuckets.js` — the grid page, its row, how rows nest and fold.
-- `AISessionDetail.js` · `AISessionConversation.js` · `AISessionCoverage.js` · `AISessionTrace.js` — a session's own page and its tabs. A clicked row opens that session's full page in place of the list (previews plus full detail views: [design/navigation](/framework/design/navigation/readme.md)); the sessions page no longer calls `columns()`.
+- `AISessionDetail.js` · `AISessionConversation.js` · `AISessionCoverage.js` · `AISessionTrace.js` — a session's own page and its tabs. A clicked row opens that session's full page in place of the list (previews plus full detail views: [design/navigation](/framework/design/navigation/readme.md)); the sessions page no longer calls `columns()`. A named agent's url (`/framework/ai/sessions/<name>/`, a `reviewer-*` or `minion-*` row) resolves the name to its session through Servex's live agent list (`AISessionDetail.agent_row`), and every load asks the folder listing first, so the page never asks for a file that is not there.
 - The session page's tabs are **Overview · Tasks · Chat**, then Coverage, Cost, Models and tokens, Related. `?tab=work` opens Tasks and `?tab=conversation` opens Chat. Above the tabs sits the sticky stats bar (`SessionStats.js`: cost, model, running for, done X of Y, the one segmented bar); it reads the tree `SessionWork` loads, so one load serves the bar, the Overview and the Tasks tab. **A session's total cost always comes from the item tool** (`AICost.ask(folder)` → `summary.cost.total`, the same cached answer as the Report tab), never from `SessionWork`'s own sum, which adds the day snapshots' older, inflated `usd`. `SessionOverview.js` draws the Overview's four cards side by side (Open, Project, Done, Dropped), with the phone's classes (`MobileRow`, `MobileTaskRow`, `mob-` CSS); `SessionTaskRow.js` is the phone's task row that opens the task's full page and shows its cost. Their styles, and the full-screen mode with two floating buttons (`AISessionDetail.full_screen`, `?full`), are `SessionOverview.css` (prefix `sov-`).
 - `SessionWork.js` (+ `.css`) — the **Tasks** tab (the old Work view; its `SessionWork.split(root)` also feeds the stats bar and the Overview): its work nested by task folder (`sessions/doc/variants/SessionTree.js` over `ai/index.json`), own and rolled cost, tasks complete of created, open tasks, the Today ▾ pill (`ux/Filter/TimeFilter`), Approve. `Approvals.js` writes `{"approve":{"at","by":"owner"}}` to the session's own `session.jsonl` plus a pointer in that day's `day.jsonl` (the line the tab streams); `Review.js` is the leak rule and its numbers (finished 1 h, over $0.50, over a day old).
 - `AISessionLive.js` · `AISessionFollow.js` · `AISessionResume.js` · `AISessionFlags.js` — live tail, follow, resume, flags.
